      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The antiarthrosic effectiveness with respect to spontaneous pain upon movement and pressure, of alclofenac (4-allyloxy-3-chlorophenyl-acetic acid) was tested in a homogeneous group of elderly patients and compared with orally administered indomethacin. The research was carried out in strictly controlled, double-blind experimental conditions. The results obtained suggest that 500 mg of the new anti-inflammatory analgesic have the same action as 25 mg of indomethacin but with a lower incidence of the side effects common to all anti-inflammatory substances. Thanks to its good tolerability and high effectiveness, the new drug should be of considerable utility in the treatment of arthrosis in the elderly and in painful, inflammatory complications."},
